{
    /* Relaxation of Laplace's equation on a grid whose boundary is held at
       zero: every sweep replaces a cell by the mean of its four neighbours.

       A mean never leaves the range of what it averages, so the values stay
       within the range they started in at every sweep. The iteration does
       converge — the update's coefficients sum to exactly 1, so not by the
       ∞-norm contraction Jacobi has, but by a spectral argument — and the
       kernel reports whether it stopped on the tolerance or on the cap.

         rhoc examples/laplace.rho --tau 1e-6 --max-iter 2000
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 32 32
    INPUT → U
    ((▷0U + ▽0U + ▷1U + ▽1U) / 4.0) ⇒ U
    U → =
}
